<title>JAPAN: Investors eye Nagoya stocks after 2005 Expo win.</title>
<headline>Investors eye Nagoya stocks after 2005 Expo win.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investors turned their attention to Nagoya-related stocks and those listed on the Nagoya bourse on Friday after a city in central Japan near Nagoya won a bid to host the 2005 World Exposition, brokers said.</p>
<p>Brokers said that there were hopes that the event would stimulate business in the area surrounding the city of Seto, where the Expo will be held.</p>
<p>As of 0500 GMT, Nagoya Railroad Co Ltd was up 22 yen at 482. Tokura Construction Co Ltd was bid-only at 553 after finishing at 478 on Thursday.</p>
</text>
